  "narrative": {
    "intro": "McKesson has $12.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. McKesson won 2,285 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $5.4M, and obligations are up 3.4% year over year. McKesson sales are concentrated in Pharmaceuticals, where Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing accounts for $12.3B. McKesson serves a small set of federal buyers at scale: the Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer with $12B in obligations, followed by the Department of Justice at $172M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $86.2M. Fiscal-year obligations have trended upward from $7.7B in FY21 to $12.3B in FY26, with a step-up to $11.9B in FY25. McKesson also shows smaller obligations in merchant wholesaler and medical manufacturing NAICS categories, including Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers at $6.3M and several small or negative entries in other markets. This profile points to a federal portfolio dominated by pharmaceutical preparation obligations and concentrated buying by the Department of Veterans Affairs.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have McKesson's federal obligations changed over time?",
        "body": "Fiscal-year obligations rose from $7.7B in FY21 to $12.3B in FY26. McKesson recorded $8.4B in FY22, $9.5B in FY23, $9B in FY24, and $11.9B in FY25. Obligations are up 3.4% year over year in the current fiscal period. The largest single NAICS market, Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing, accounts for $12.3B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are McKesson's largest federal customers and what markets do they buy?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $12B. The Department of Justice obligated $172M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $86.2M; the Department of Homeland Security obligated $18.6M and the Peace Corps obligated $437K. McKesson's principal market is Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing at $12.3B, with smaller activity in Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers at $6.3M and minor entries in other NAICS categories."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does McKesson make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "McKesson has $12.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. McKesson received 2,285 awards in the current fiscal period, with an average award size of $5.4M. Obligations are up 3.4% year over year compared with the prior-year period."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from McKesson?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is McKesson's largest federal customer with $12B in obligations. The Department of Justice follows with $172M, and the Department of Health and Human Services follows with $86.2M; other buyers include the Department of Homeland Security at $18.6M and the Peace Corps at $437K. The Department of State shows $0 in obligations."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does McKesson sell to the government?",
      "a": "McKesson sells primarily pharmaceutical products, reflected by Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing at $12.3B. McKesson also has obligations in Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers at $6.3M and several smaller or negative-value entries in other medical manufacturing and wholesaling NAICS categories."
    },
